 # Repository Maintenance Guide
 
+## Dedicated Hermes operating brief
+
+This repository belongs only to the **Advanced Transportation Update** Hermes
+project/profile (`advtransport`). It is not part of the novelwriting project and
+must never inherit novelwriting roles, goals, prompts, or files.
+
+The dedicated master brief is
+`docs/HERMES_MASTER_OPERATING_INSTRUCTIONS.md`. Its persistent goal and
+Detailed Architecture and Workflow Appendix are authoritative, together with
+the compact profile SOUL and the repository-specific safeguards below. Inspect
+its headings and read the relevant section when a stage or requirement needs
+clarification; do not load the entire long document into model context on every
+run. If instructions differ, apply the more restrictive publication, delivery,
+credential, and human-authorization rule.
+
+Never alter or operate the separate ChatGPT Advanced Transportation automation
+from this repository. Never send email, publish, activate a schedule, change
+credentials, or push changes unless the user has explicitly authorized that
+specific action.
+
+### Current Hermes delivery authorization (2026-10-14)
+
+The user has explicitly authorized the dedicated Hermes workflow to:
+
+- run automatically under Hermes control;
+- monitor public sources continuously without using or depending on the ETTE
+  email;
+- prepare one edition each weekday, with a target delivery time of 9:30 a.m.
+  Eastern after all required AI, validation, and QC stages finish;
+- treat Monday as the Weekend + Monday edition, including developments since
+  the prior Friday edition; and
+- send the validated multipart edition from
+  `advancedtransportationupdate@gmail.com` to
+  `advancedtransportationupdate@gmail.com` through the Gmail account linked to
+  Hermes, with duplicate-send protection and provider confirmation.
+
+This authorization does not extend to changing, pausing, replacing, or
+stopping the separate ChatGPT Advanced Transportation automation, which must
+continue independently until the user explicitly says otherwise. It also does
+not authorize using the ETTE email as an input to the Hermes edition.
+
+### Current Hermes website-publication authorization (2026-10-15)
+
+The owner explicitly authorized Hermes to publish each validated weekday edition
+to the existing GitHub Pages site at `news.peterjwhite.org`. After deterministic
+QC passes, Hermes may commit only `data/latest_briefing.json` and the matching
+`data/archive/YYYY-MM-DD.json` to `main`. Use
+`scripts/publish_validated_site.py`; it builds the commit from `origin/main` and
+must not include any other working-tree change. Never overwrite a conflicting
+dated archive, publish a failed or incomplete edition, alter DNS or hosting, or
+touch the separate ChatGPT automation.
+
+For large daily candidate sets, do not repeatedly load or print the complete
+inventory into model context. Review it once, then use deterministic code to
+score, deduplicate, and save a compact, section-balanced shortlist with source
+indices and URLs in the dated run directory. Continue drafting and QC from that
+saved shortlist. Preserve successful stage artifacts and never restart an
+earlier stage merely because later context was compressed.
+
+### Mandatory one-or-two-sentence article summaries (2026-10-15)
+
+Every published article must have one or two complete explanatory sentences
+immediately beneath its headline. State the verified development and explain its
+significance for advanced transportation, policy, safety, deployment, industry,
+or operations; use one concise sentence when it covers both, otherwise use two.
+Do not repeat the headline, use filler, expose editorial process language, or
+leave a summary blank. The final
+independent QC must run `scripts/final_summary_qc.py` against the dated JSON,
+HTML, and plain-text artifacts. Any missing or three-plus-sentence summary, or
+any summary not rendered in both output formats, blocks website
+publication and email delivery.
+
